-- expected_rows --
[]
-- description --
histogram_quantile over min_over_time of a classic bucket selector, with no aggregation, one quantile per series.
Prometheus reads each `le` rung of a classic histogram as an ordinary float
series, so min_over_time reduces every rung to the smallest cumulative count in the window
before the quantile interpolates the ladder. Series `a` carries three samples
of one layout; series `b` carries two, the newer with its top finite bound
moved from 4 to 3, so its `le="4"` and `le="3"` rungs each hold one sample.
The unequal sample counts and the layout change make avg_over_time,
max_over_time, min_over_time, last_over_time and sum_over_time answer five
different quantiles, aggregated and per series.
